 ## Background
-NLR (Neural Lumigraph Representation) was introduced as a method for novel view synthesis using neural networks [S1, unofficial]. The baseline implementation was provided by the original authors [S1, unofficial]. MetaNLR was developed to improve few-shot learning capabilities by applying Reptile meta-learning to the NLR initialization [S1, unofficial].
+The source does not provide publication dates or original authors beyond referencing [3] for NLR and [10] for Reptile [S1, unofficial]. The baseline implementation was accessed directly from the NLR authors [S1, unofficial]. MetaNLR applies an outer Reptile meta-learning loop to learn the initialization of the shape and color networks [S1, unofficial].
 
